
  caboose apply  environment default
  1 proposal from sessions in the sandbox. Each is shown whole, and nothing
  changes until you say so. ^C stops; what was applied before it stays.

  Keep the host awake                                                      1/1
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  long builds

  awake.toml, proposed 1h ago

  A host command the sandbox may run ([alias.awake]), with caboose-agent run
  awake:
    command  TMP/bin/awake
             -i {mode}
    in       a fresh empty directory
    {mode}   idle, disk

    --- TMP/.caboose/envs/default/config.toml
    +++ with the alias
      #[ref.default]
      #image = "debian:13.7-slim"
    + 
    + [alias.awake]
    + command = ["TMP/bin/awake", "-i", "{mode}"]
    + description = "keep it awake"
    + policy = "ask"
    + 
    + [alias.awake.params]
    + mode = ["idle", "disk"]


  ? Apply this proposal?
    1  Apply it
    2  Leave it pending
    3  Delete it
    choose 1-3 [2]:   ? To let the sandbox run
    TMP/bin/awake
